# Git Branching and Merging Lab
## Branch Creation
### Create a new branch
```bash
git branch GitNewBranch
```
### Check available branches
```bash
git branch
```
To view local and remote branches:
```bash
git branch -a
```
### Switch to the new branch
```bash
git checkout GitNewBranch
```
---
## Create a Sample File
Create a file:
```bash
echo "Branch File" > branch.txt
```
Check the file:
```bash
cat branch.txt
```
---
## Save the Changes
Add the file:
```bash
git add branch.txt
```
Commit the changes:
```bash
git commit -m "Added branch file"
``
Check repository status:
```bash
git status
```
---
## Merge with Main Branch
Switch to the main branch:
```bash
git checkout main
```
If your repository uses `master`:
```bash
git checkout master
```
---
## Compare Branches
Show command-line differences:
```bash
git diff main GitNewBranch
```
or
```bash
git diff master GitNewBranch
```
---
## Merge Branch
Merge the new branch into the main branch:
```bash
git merge GitNewBranch
```
---
## View Commit History
```bash
git log --oneline --graph --decorate
```
---
## Delete the Branch
```bash
git branch -d GitNewBranch
```
---
## Final Check
```bash
git status
```
---
